  "status": "double-checked",
  "note": "Read from page images (scanned PDF, no text layer). Every table and chart value was read twice on differently cropped renders (pass A: scale 2.78, left and right halves; pass B: scale 3.0, top and bottom halves, or zoomed sub-crops for charts) and recorded only when both passes agreed; chart labels whose digits overprint each other were left out (listed in excluded). Chart labels were assigned to bars by checking on the rendered chart that each label sits over its own bar in legend order and that label order matches bar heights; isolate-weighted chart values reconcile with each table's overall %R. Row n for charts from the legend counts, which sum to the table's blood N with the stated outpatient remainder. Page numbers are PDF page numbers (printed page number plus 1)."
 },
 "notes": "Second annual report of TARS-Net (state network under NCDC's National Programme on AMR Containment, nodal centre Osmania Medical College, Hyderabad): 13 sites, 15,752 priority-pathogen isolates, 14,616 after removing duplicates. Values are % resistant as printed. Genus-level organisms as printed (Klebsiella, Pseudomonas, Acinetobacter and Enterococcus species). Pus aspirate (NCDC definition: aspirated purulent material from a closed infected site; the tables label it PUS) is mapped to deep, the brief's key for aspirates; other sterile body fluids (OSBF) to sterile. Chart rows: IN (inpatients, emergency included per the Figure 3 footnote) mapped to ward. Source inconsistencies kept as printed: the OSBF N in the headers of Tables 6, 7 and 11 (18, 38, 96) do not match the count tables (38, 18, 59); Table 8 marks ampicillin for blood as not tested while Figure 7 plots it; Figure 6 footnote gives 217 blood isolates against a caption of 208.",
